phie Wilson"}],"groups":null,"members":null,"namevariations":["Wilow"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/4299757-Willow-18","type":"artist","urls":["https://www.instagram.com/willow.mcr","https://x.com/WillowMcr","https://willowsoundesign.bandcamp.com/","https://linktr.ee/willowdj","https://soundcloud.com/willowmcr","http://www.residentadvisor.net/dj/willow","https://goout.net/en/willow/pzfipxf/"]}},"/api/discogs/artist/66916/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"66916","image":"https://i.discogs.com/9KI64wMWFiSm4xOmDBZEk0-0okRbrHeRoa7PrBs5ZjE/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:387/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY2OTE2/LTE1MTc2Njk5MDct/NTEyMS5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/Tgw-wb2Zeyvk5tPSojoH2l61MkgivvM2c7SrS6PGlLk/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9BLTY2OTE2/LTE1MTc2Njk5MDct/NTEyMS5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"British Rock studio project initially formed to record a concept album about Edgar Allan Poe. They became best known for the power ballad \"Eye in the Sky\" and the instrumental \"Sirius\".\r\n\r\n[b]Official band members[/b]\r\n● [a=Alan Parsons] – production, engineering, programming, composition, keyboards, guitar\r\n● [a=Eric Woolfson] – composition, lyrics, piano, keyboards, vocals, executive production\r\n\r\n[b]Notable contributors[/b]\r\n● [a=Andrew Powell] – composition, keyboards, orchestral arrangements (1975-1990)\r\n● [a=Philharmonia Orchestra]\r\n● [a=The English Chorale] – choir (1976, 1977, 1982, 1987)\r\n● [a=Ian Bairnson] – guitar (1975–1990)\r\n● [a=David Pack] – guitar (1976)\r\n● [a=David Paton] – bass, vocals (1975–1985)\r\n● [a=Duncan Mackay] – keyboards (1977–1979)\r\n● [a=Richard Cottle] – keyboards, saxophone (1984–1990)\r\n● [a=Laurence Cottle] – bass (1987-1990)\r\n● [a=Stuart Tosh] – drums, percussion (1975–1976)\r\n● [a=Stuart Elliott] – drums, percussion (1977–1990)\r\n● [a=John Leach] – cimbalom, kantele (1976–1978)\r\n● [a=Colin Blunstone] – vocals (1978–1984)\r\n● [a=Chris Rainbow] – vocals (1979–1990)\r\n● [a=Lenny Zakatek] – vocals (1977–1987)\r\n● [a=John Miles] – vocals (1976, 1978, 1985, 1987)\r\n● [a=Jack Harris] – vocals (1976–1978)\r\n● [a=Dave Townsend] – vocals (1977, 1979)\r\n● [a=Elmer Gantry] a.k.a. [a=Dave Terry (4)] – vocals (1980, 1982)\r\n● [a=Graham Dye] – vocals (1985, 1990)\r\n\r\nNon-recurring vocalists include: [a=Arthur Brown] (1975), [a=Allan Clarke] (1977), [a=Peter Straker] (1977), [a=Jaki Whitren] (1977), [a=Dean Ford] (1978), [a=Clare Torry] (1979), [a=Lesley Duncan] (1979), [a=Gary Brooker] (1985), [a=Geoff Barradale] (1987), [a=Eric Stewart] (1990)\r\n\r\nNotable instruments: Projectron - A device built by Alan Parsons as an analog sample playback device, similar in general concept to a Mellotron. The Projectron consisted of a 24-track tape machine, with each playback channel routed to a voltage controlled amplifier; each VCA was in turn gated by a key of an attached keyboard. The device was used on the albums I Robot, Pyramid, and The Turn of a Friendly Card. But preparing tapes was a cumbersome process and the device was maintenance-intensive, so as soon as a Fairlight CMI became available to Parsons, he switched his sampling activities to that. Parsons scrapped the Projectron sometime after 1980, and no photos of it are known to have survived.","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:artist:66916","relations":{"aliases":null,"groups":null,"members":[{"active":true,"id":157075,"name":"Alan Parsons"},{"active":true,"id":218601,"name":"Eric Woolfson"}],"namevariations":["A. Parson","A. Parsons","A.P.P.","A.Parsons","Alan Arson","Alan Parson","Alan Parson Project","Alan Parson's Project","Alan Parson's Proyect","Alan Parsons","Alan Parsons P.","Alan Parsons Project","Allan Parsons Project","El Proyecto De Alan Parsons","T.A.P.P.","The Alan Parson","The Alan Parson Project","The Alan Parson's Project","The Alan Parsons","The Alan Parsons Projekt","The Allan Parsons Project","« The Alan Parsons Project »","Алан Парсонс Проджект","アラン・パーソンズ・プロジェクト","亞倫派森合唱團","亞倫派森計劃","알란 파슨스 프로젝트"]},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/artist/66916-The-Alan-Parsons-Project","type":"artist","urls":["https://alanparsons.com/","http://amiright.com/artists/alanparsonsproject.shtml","https://www.facebook.com/TheAlanParsonsProject","https://www.the-alan-parsons-project.com/","https://genius.com/artists/The-alan-parsons-project","https://www.last.fm/music/The+Alan+Parsons+Project","https://www.progarchives.com/artist.asp?id=286","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Alan_Parsons_Project","https://www.imdb.com/name/nm1721338/","https://www.allmusic.com/artist/the-alan-parsons-project-mn0001176481"]}},"/api/discogs/label/1233122/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"1233122","image":"https://i.discogs.com/B0cSngkTeV0Vkvw_2iTTi5ol2JuRVLkeLB8qyj5T_Zg/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:588/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEyMzMx/MjItMTcxMzk3NTQy/OC05NzMzLmpwZWc.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/ZpsXzkFCZpvEMq59gAcswP8PGD4HJ3HjHTL2TNHKMXM/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEyMzMx/MjItMTcxMzk3NTQy/OC05NzMzLmpwZWc.jpeg","profile":"","provider":"discogs","ref":"discogs:label:1233122","relations":{"parentLabel":null,"sublabels":null},"schemaVersion":2,"sourceUrl":"https://www.discogs.com/label/1233122-Asking-For-Trouble-2","type":"label","urls":[]}},"/api/discogs/label/13768/profile":{"cached":true,"profile":{"id":"13768","image":"https://i.discogs.com/fkWr4UykQKmJOYOKxyEsWf9r0suHa4FvZiwq-FDFknA/rs:fit/g:sm/q:90/h:600/w:600/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEzNzY4/LTE3NzAwNTA5NTQt/ODAyNy5qcGVn.jpeg","imageThumb":"https://i.discogs.com/DqxJBqKgV4fXuHuNo2KX1ylMJCOVcnI8SqlsMYvZT4g/rs:fit/g:sm/q:40/h:150/w:150/czM6Ly9kaXNjb2dz/LWRhdGFiYXNlLWlt/YWdlcy9MLTEzNzY4/LTE3NzAwNTA5NTQt/ODAyNy5qcGVn.jpeg","profile":"Brazilian Label with a Portuguese branch. In Brazil belonging to the communications conglomerate Grupo G